      "provenance": {
        "notes": "NAME CLASH: false jasmine, not a Jasminum (row 73 is Jasminum officinale, row 200 is this plant). Starter list says search-summary only; now read from fetched RHS growing guide and NC State page. Watering: RHS says pots dry out fast and must neither dry out nor waterlog; in the ground only first-year and dry-spell watering, so style keep_moist is the pot reading. Interval 5 days is a guess. Light: RHS warm sheltered sun or light shade; NC State full sun to partial shade; stored bright_indirect as the closest class. Size: RHS says slow-growing, 4 m or more eventually, no spread; NC State says 3 to 20 ft by 3 to 4 ft and rapid growth, so the RHS and NC State disagree on speed; height 400 is the RHS figure, spread 100 is a mapping of NC State's 3 to 4 ft, hence from_knowledge_verify; growth rate left unknown. Hardiness: RHS gives no rating and says protect in frost; NC State zones 8a to 10b, container overwintered indoors in colder climates; no temperature stored. Toxicity: ASPCA lists T. jasminoides non-toxic to cats and dogs (severity 0 graded by us). NC State is mixed: plant type says Poisonous but its tags say non-toxic for cats and dogs, with no explanation; it also notes milky latex sap. Stored severity 0 with this conflict recorded; skin irritation from the sap is not graded. Es and it names are author knowledge (machine draft), not fetched."
      },
